                  "value": {
                    "stringValue": "[{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"parts\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"content\":\"An **agent trace** is a record of what an AI agent did while handling a task. It may include the steps it took, tool calls it made, results it received, and its final response.\\n\\nFor example:\\n\\n1. User asks for the weather.\\n2. Agent calls a weather service for the user\u2019s city.\\n3. Service returns the forecast.\\n4. Agent summarizes it for the user.\\n\\nTraces help people debug, evaluate, and audit an agent\u2019s behavior. A trace is not necessarily the agent\u2019s private reasoning: it can show actions and results without exposing hidden internal reasoning.\"}],\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}]"
